format: 2
name: JulcMap lookup with an equal byte[] key (T10)
class: Probe
method: m
arg: a142010201
arg: 420102
expect: AGREE
note: Off-chain JulcAssocMap compares keys with Objects.equals, so an equal but distinct byte[] is not found.
note: ADR-068 M1 (D6) makes JuLC's JVM collections compare byte[] elements, keys and values by content, as on-chain,
note: so the JVM now finds the key and the case agrees at every level; recorded.jvm and recorded.base keep the old
note: pins. T10's record-with-byte[]-component form stays open (ADR-068 D6, JULC0087 in M3).
recorded.jvm: Value d87980 []
recorded.base: Value d87a80 []
---
import java.math.BigInteger;
import org.julclang.core.types.JulcList;
import org.julclang.core.types.JulcMap;

public class Probe {
    public static boolean m(JulcMap<byte[], BigInteger> map, byte[] key) {
        return map.containsKey(key);
    }
}
